# Client-Side & Frontend Security Sub-Skill

When invoked standalone or by `security-orchestrator`, systematically audit frontend and client-side code:

## 1. DOM-based XSS (Cross-Site Scripting)
- Check dangerous DOM sinks: `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`, `innerHTML`, `document.write()`, `eval()`, `v-html`.
- Verify user input passing into client-side dynamic evaluation or unescaped HTML injection.

## 2. Insecure Client Storage & Secrets
- Check for sensitive data (Tokens, Passwords, PII, API Keys) stored in `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, or `document.cookie` without `HttpOnly` flags.

## 3. Client-Side Authentication & Routing Bypass
- Check if critical UI components or admin views rely solely on client-side state (e.g. `isLoggedIn`, `isAdmin` in React/Vue state) without backend verification.

## 4. Open Redirects & Clickjacking
- Audit dynamic client-side redirects (`window.location.href = userInput`) for open redirect vulnerabilities.
- Check frame options & Content Security Policy (CSP) headers against Clickjacking.

## 5. Web Security Headers & CSP
- Verify Content Security Policy (CSP), CORS (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin`), and Resource Sharing rules.
